WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:12.500
We move now to the agenda items relating to
our various committee reports.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.230
Two reports there.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:17.350
I think they are both self-evident.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.070
I would not suggest adding anything.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.840
Thank you very much.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:29.460
We have Investment Committee and Audit and
Risk.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:37.760
We had a conversation on Monday that will
be documented for the next Board, Chairman.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.760
I would suggest we cover it then.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.760
Thank you very much.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.700
That brings me to any other business.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.550
We have the date of the next meeting; I have
one item of other business.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:50.650
Can I just check whether anybody else has
any items of other business?

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.510
Yes, there was one item.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:01:00.030
It is just to let the Board know that, this
afternoon, NHS England will be publishing

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:06.940
the report of the independent investigation
into learning disability deaths at Southern

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:08.080
Health Foundation Trust.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.190
Jane may want to say a word in a moment.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:17.520
This was a report that we commissioned following
the death of a young man, Connor Sparrowhawk,

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.299
in July 2013 in a unit in Oxford.

00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:30.840
The report, which produces recommendations
for the trust, for CCGs and for NHS Improvement,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:36.790
CQC and ourselves, is being accepted, and
it contains a number of important recommendations

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:41.810
which sync up with the work that we already
have underway around the national Learning

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.540
Disability Mortality Review.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:48.729
I will not say more ahead of the publication
of the report this afternoon, but this is

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:54.130
an important and serious set of findings that
need to be acted on.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:59.490
The three national bodies – CQC and ourselves,
with NHS Improvement – will be doing so.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:05.409
NHS Improvement, as the regulator, has particular
responsibilities in respect of this trust,

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:07.030
and will be acting accordingly.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:09.460
Jane, I do not know if you wanted to add to
that?

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.610
I do not think so, Simon.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.780
You have set out the position completely.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:20.999
The only thing I would add is that we have
established a helpline, which is up and running

00:02:20.999 --> 00:02:26.549
and will continue to run, for anybody that
is concerned or wants to ask for further information.

00:02:26.549 --> 00:02:31.549
That is already established, and we have the
details of that already available.

00:02:31.549 --> 00:02:37.519
We will reinforce that later this afternoon.

00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:39.489
One other thing, unrelated to that.

00:02:39.489 --> 00:02:45.549
Just to respond to some of the questions that
might have been forming in people’s minds

00:02:45.549 --> 00:02:49.719
following the allocations discussion that
we had: I think it is worth clarifying that

00:02:49.719 --> 00:02:57.059
the pace-of-change option that the Board has
chosen is obviously a pro-equity pace change

00:02:57.059 --> 00:02:58.439
allocation.

00:02:58.439 --> 00:03:04.719
Therefore, some of the most outlying CCGs
may not be getting real-terms increases on

00:03:04.719 --> 00:03:09.069
the core CCG allocations, but I think it is
worth clarifying that, when you take account

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:14.079
of the Sustainability and Transformation Fund
investment which we expect that they will

00:03:14.079 --> 00:03:21.330
receive, then in fact every CCG will be receiving,
for their people, real terms funding increases

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.510
in 2016/2017, and that is likely to be the
position thereafter, too.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:29.530
That is just to clarify, should that doubt
have formed in people’s minds.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:30.530
Good.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:31.530
Thank you very much, Simon.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:38.819
In a moment, I am going to ask the Board to
record thanks to three members of the Board

00:03:38.819 --> 00:03:42.260
who are standing down, and for whom this is
the last meeting.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.390
That is Tim, Ciarán and Barbara.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:52.939
Just in case there is any resistance to that
proposal, let me just say a few words about

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:54.180
them.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:59.709
Tim and Ciarán and Barbara have all been
with us almost from the very beginning, so

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:02.510
this is quite a change moment for us as a
Board.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:06.670
They have been pivotal members of the Board,
all three of them.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:11.980
Tim has brought to us, I think, an enormous
intellectual energy and drive, and a capacity

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:19.000
for disruption which is hugely welcomed in
a very stable system such as this.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:25.450
He has been the father of progeny which has
grown, but not yet grown into adulthood, by

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:30.540
which I mean the digitisation of a service
which we know will ultimately transform what

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.330
we are able to do for patients.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:41.540
Tim, you are our Christmas gift to the people
of Australia, and we wish you every good wish

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.130
for your time with Telstra Health.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:48.580
We know that you will thrive and have a very
fulfilling time there.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:57.450
Ciarán is one of the founding fathers of
NHS England, and has been an immensely powerful

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:03.260
influence on us, I think, in bringing us back
to earth about how everything that we do,

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:07.330
even at the high levels when we talk about
allocations, comes back to patients and comes

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:08.350
back to people.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:12.990
Also I think, as he has done today, he convinces
us that actually it is not all about money,

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:13.990
stupid.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:14.990
It is actually about behaviours.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:22.590
It is actually about how we influence the
way in which humans, and the therapists and

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:28.240
the clinical people who deal with them, behave
in order to produce hugely enhanced health

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.240
outcomes.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:33.570
Ciarán’s term of office has come to an
end, and unfortunately the British Council

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:40.460
have snapped him up and put him into an aircraft
where, even from 35,000 feet, he has not been

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.410
able to continue with us.

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:45.480
Ciarán, we are very grateful for everything
you have done.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:50.150
Although Barbara has been with us and NHS
England since the beginning, she has been

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:53.070
with the NHS almost, I think, since the beginning
of the NHS.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:06:00.250
That was a low blow!

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:05.160
As lawyers say, ‘As memory knoweth not to
the contrary,’ so great has been her influence;

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:13.210
certainly for over 41 years, I think, as a
GP and increasingly as a manager: coming into

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:19.320
PCTs, into SHA and then, in the fullness of
time, blossoming from that background into

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.420
NHS England.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:26.190
I have to say personally that she has been
an extraordinary mentor to me, and has done

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:31.490
her very best to dispel the clouds of ignorance
which still swirl around my head in relation

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:32.720
to the NHS.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:37.850
Barbara, as your report today demonstrated,
you are somebody who is in charge of operations,

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:42.870
somebody who delivers and who has had a huge
loyalty across the whole of the workforce

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:46.590
who report to you, and much more broadly out
into the NHS.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.520
We all owe you an enormous debt of gratitude.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.520
I am not going to ask them to respond.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:59.240
What I am going to ask is: is that sufficient
to persuade the Board to offer our warmest

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:09.530
thanks for everything these three have done,
and our very best wishes for their future?

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:15.090
On that note I declare the meeting closed
and I ask the Board to past the usual resolution

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:18.370
as to our conduct to close business.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.139
Thank you very much everybody who joined us
this morning.

